{"type": "message", "id": "66d04585", "parentId": "f832cee1", "timestamp": "2026-04-10T10:01:44.695Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "toolu_bdrk_01XjGycC5vfhNeJbY8P6dsCE", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"5 most deadly cancers death rate 5-year survival rate US 2024 2025\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 974,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"38dc10d77c0b4997\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAL 30,030 AZ 42,560 AR 19,700 CA 199,980 CO 29,020 CT 23,920 DE 7,680 FL\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"38dc10d77c0b4997\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.cancer.org/content/dam/cancer-org/research/cancer-facts-and-statistics/annual-cancer-facts-and-figures/2025/2025-cancer-facts-and-figures-acs.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ebe60b64e64e061c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nData source: Surveillance, Epidemiology, and End Results (SEER) Program, National Cancer Institute, 2024. ©2025, American Cancer Society, Inc., Surveillance and Health Equity Science ... Burkitt lymphoma. ... Table 8. Five-year Relative Survival Rates (%) by Stage at Diagnosis, 2014-2020\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ebe60b64e64e061c\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.cancer.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a0b6458d87718feb\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nCancer Stat Facts: Common Cancer Sites - SEER\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a0b6458d87718feb\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://seer.cancer.gov/statfacts/html/common.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"87048bdac27b955a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n<strong>Lung and bronchus cancer</strong> is responsible for the most deaths with 124,730 people expected to die from this disease. That is nearly three times the 52,900 deaths due to colorectal cancer, which is the second most common cause of cancer death.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"87048bdac27b955a\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"seer.cancer.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fb18ba90d9f83140\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nCancer Statistics - NCI\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fb18ba90d9f83140\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.cancer.gov/about-cancer/understanding/statistics\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d6bfbd39c4497a9e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe most recent Annual Report to the Nation on the Status of Cancer, released in April 2025, shows that overall cancer death rates decreased by: ... Although death rates for many individual cancer types have also declined, rates for a few cancers have not changed or even increased. As the overall cancer death rate has declined, the number of cancer survivors has increased.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d6bfbd39c4497a9e\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.cancer.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d77612c5ee6ed806\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nWhat Are the Deadliest Cancers?\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d77612c5ee6ed806\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.verywellhealth.com/top-deadliest-cancers-1123927\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c6b8f94f09735fa6\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe most deadly types of cancers include <strong>lung, colon, pancreatic cancer, breast, and prostate cancers</strong>. Keep in mind that estimated deaths can vary between males and females and may be affected by age and family history.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c6b8f94f09735fa6\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"April 14, 2015\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.verywellhealth.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"befd5a4ba11a1134\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAmerican Cancer Society Study Projects 2024 Cancer Incidence and Mortality | CancerNetwork\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"befd5a4ba11a1134\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.cancernetwork.com/view/american-cancer-society-study-projects-2024-cancer-incidence-and-mortality\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b53dec14f36c5a4e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nFrom the mid-1970s to 2013 to 2019, the 5-year survival rate for all cancers had increased from 49% to 69%. Survival rates were highest among those with <strong>thyroid (99%), prostate (97%), and testis cancer (95%) as well as melanoma (94%).</strong>\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b53dec14f36c5a4e\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"3 weeks ago\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.cancernetwork.com\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "5 most deadly cancers death rate 5-year survival rate US 2024 2025", "provider": "brave", "count": 5, "tookMs": 974, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"38dc10d77c0b4997\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nAL 30,030 AZ 42,560 AR 19,700 CA 199,980 CO 29,020 CT 23,920 DE 7,680 FL\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"38dc10d77c0b4997\">>>", "url": "https://www.cancer.org/content/dam/cancer-org/research/cancer-facts-and-statistics/annual-cancer-facts-and-figures/2025/2025-cancer-facts-and-figures-acs.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ebe60b64e64e061c\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nData source: Surveillance, Epidemiology, and End Results (SEER) Program, National Cancer Institute, 2024. ©2025, American Cancer Society, Inc., Surveillance and Health Equity Science ... Burkitt lymphoma. ... 