ederal statistics on cancer incidence and population data for all 50 states and the District of Columbia [7]. International Classification of Diseases (ICD) for Oncology, third edition code data was extracted for cholangiocarcinoma (8160/3). Incidence data were stratified based on sex, race, stage, primary location (intrahepatic bile duct or extrahepatic bile duct), and US regions (Northeast, Midwest, South, and West).\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ad4142acc6a1996f\">>>", "siteName": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov"}]}, "isError": false, "timestamp": 1775815320948}}
